Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that

$$
\begin{aligned}T(-kv+hw)=T(-kv)+T(hw)=-kT(v)+hT(w)\end{aligned}
$$

for any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}T(-6{v}_{1}+5{v}_{2}) & =-6T({v}_{1})+5T({v}_{2}) \\ [\begin{aligned}8 \\ -39\end{aligned}] & =-6T({v}_{1})+5[\begin{aligned}4 \\ -3\end{aligned}] \\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =5[\begin{aligned}4 \\ -3\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}8 \\ -39\end{aligned}] \\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}20 \\ -15\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}8 \\ -39\end{aligned}] \\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}12 \\ 24\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =\frac{1}{6}[\begin{aligned}12 \\ 24\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}2 \\ 4\end{aligned}].\end{aligned}
$$
